<title>FRANCE: French bank CCF soars more than 10 pct.</title>
<headline>French bank CCF soars more than 10 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trading in French CCF bank shares was temporarily suspended on Wednesday under stock market rules which impose a brief cooling-off period for shares which jump by 10 percent or more.</p>
<p>The stock re-quoted at 1000 GMT with wider upward margins and was up 10.59 percent at 289.2 francs at 1002 GMT.</p>
<p>Banking stocks have been roaring ahead this week on renewed sector restructuring speculation in the wake of a German bank merger.</p>
<p>The CAC-40 leading share index hit a new all-time high on Wednesday. Other bank stocks were surging too.</p>
</text>
